  <title>SET DATE Command</title>
  <keywords>
    <keyword>Commands</keyword>
    <keyword>Dates<keyword>setting date format</keyword></keyword>
    <keyword>SET DATE command</keyword>
    <keyword>SET DATE TO command</keyword>
    <keyword>Setting<keyword>date formats</keyword></keyword>
  </keywords>
  <body>
    <header>
      <para styleclass="Heading1">SET DATE Command</para>
    </header>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><snippet src="__CommandInclude" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">用途</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">Change the setting that determines the &lt;%APP%&gt; date format by selecting from a list of constants with corresponding date formats.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">语法</para>
    <para styleclass="Code with box">SET DATE [TO] &lt;kCountrySetting&gt;</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">参数</para>
    <para styleclass="List"><text styleclass="Italic">kCountrySetting</text><tab/>One of the following keywords:<br/>AMERICAN or MDY (MM/DD/YY)<br/>ANSI (YY.MM.DD)<br/>BRITISH or DMY (DD/MM/YY)<br/>FRENCH (DD/MM/YY)<br/>GERMAN (DD.MM.YY)<br/>ITALIAN or DUTCH (DD-MM-YY)<br/>JAPANESE, TAIWAN or YMD (YY/MM/DD)<br/>USA (MM-DD-YY)<br/>SYSTEM or WINDOWS (the format of the Windows regional settings)<br/>A macro (&amp;) that evaluates to a date format string, such as DD.MM.YYYY, is passed to SetDateFormat().</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Description</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">SET DATE is functionally equivalent to SetDateCountry().  </para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Examples</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">This example illustrates various system-defined country settings:</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"></para>
    <para styleclass="Code Example">SET DATE German<br/>? Today()<tab/><tab/><tab/><tab/>// Result:  15.10.19<br/>SET DATE Ansi<br/>? Today()<tab/><tab/><tab/><tab/>// Result:  19.10.15</para>
    <para styleclass="Body Text"><snippet src="__IncludeLibRt" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">参见</para>
